          </h2>

          <p>
            Manufacturers publish sizing charts that match capacity to floor area and dampness, and the charts broadly agree. The figures below are typical of those charts for the current DOE ratings, not our own measurements, so treat them as a starting point. Ceiling height, open-plan layouts and how much laundry or cooking happens in the space all push the right answer upwards.
          </p>

