          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The right dehumidifier for your home is mostly a sizing decision. Pick 22, 35 or 50 pints on the current DOE scale, make sure it can drain by hose, and set it to a sensible target rather than the lowest number it offers. For most ordinary houses, the Frigidaire 35-pint is the place to start, and the Midea Cube earns its premium only if you will use the app.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Be honest about the cause, too. If the bucket fills faster than the weather explains, you have a water-entry problem, and the machine is only treating the symptom. Fix the source, use the dehumidifier for what remains, and keep a cheap hygrometer in the room so you know whether it is working.
